  "doc": "I27 prereg sidecar (BUILD_PLAN I27 'Preregister': the detected pairs, the residues at LCI+1, their static classification, the laws and their outcomes, computed in the prereg from the committed extracted documents). Computed at the prereg by tests_m3/test_undo.py::undo_basis_doc (rules U1-U6 and D1-D3 of that file's docstring, written out a second time, independently of holon/) from the inputs listed with their sha256: the UNDO sidecar (spec/M3/lib/undo.json), the model sidecar it names (spec/M3/lib/sort_types.json, I30's: the documents), the adopted extracted rollup document (spec/M2/facts/morph_rollup.extracted.json, I19/A19, Q19), the planted mutant and its extraction sidecar (tests_m3/fixtures/undo/mutant/), and results/M1/L_undo_*.json (the back-test's M1 statuses). How each value was computed: (1) pins (U2): every top-level conjunct of every guard reach that fixes a whole register to a literal; (2) restores (U3): for every ordered pair of distinct state-changing actions, every final write of a whose register a pins (literal, zero) or advances by a literal under its own guard's equality with the cursor (cursor), undone by an unconditional write of the other action (the literal, or the cursor moved back by the same literal); (3) pairs (U4): the restoring pairs with at least one of the three criteria of whitepaper section 5.2 (guard, cursor, inverse event); the others are listed as rejected; (4) residues (U5): a's final writes neither restored nor identity copies; (5) residue bases (U6): one per (undo action, family), with the cursors the undo restores and the mapping families it zeroes unconditionally; (6) static classes (D1-D3): every read of the residue family in every action, views included, excluded when its key is at or below a cursor (D1), dominated by a guard requiring a zeroed family nonzero at the same key (D2) or masked inside a conjunction by such a conjunct (D3); live otherwise; (7) laws (L1, L2): one pair law per pair and one residue law per residue basis, predicted PROVED iff statically dead (the plan's exit: static and kernel classifications agree); (8) backtest: the frozen map of spec/M3/lib/undo.json applied to the M1 UNDO laws; (9) sensitivity: the same rules over the Rollup mutant without Rollup.sol:447. The build never reads this file; the tests compare holon's outputs with it, and recompute it to check it was not edited.",
